00:10:11.089 --> 00:10:15.429
You buy shares of a royalty company the day after it announces a guidance increase tied

00:10:15.429 --> 00:10:16.589
to higher gold prices.

00:10:17.169 --> 00:10:20.649
The stock rises, and the percentage gain outruns the move in the metal.

00:10:21.229 --> 00:10:21.949
What would you do?

00:10:22.309 --> 00:10:26.369
Fade it as an overreaction, or treat the gap as the taxi fare structure working.

00:10:26.369 --> 00:10:31.829
Royalty Agreements grant the holder a percentage of revenue or a fixed payment per ounce from a

00:10:31.829 --> 00:10:36.609
producing mine without any responsibility for capital expenditures or operating losses.

00:10:37.089 --> 00:10:41.669
When the gold price rises, the royalty cash flow increases almost dollar for dollar

00:10:41.669 --> 00:10:47.269
while the operator absorbs the fixed costs, which is operating leverage for the holder rather than

00:10:47.269 --> 00:10:52.309
for the miner. The common misconception is that royalty companies behave like leveraged miners.

00:10:52.309 --> 00:10:56.809
in reality, their margins expand faster than miners because they carry no

00:10:56.809 --> 00:11:01.189
sustaining capital or labor costs. Compare the royalty company's enterprise

00:11:01.189 --> 00:11:05.529
value per attributable ounce against the broader minor peer group. That is

00:11:05.529 --> 00:11:09.989
the royalty screen by name, and you can quantify the margin advantage embedded in

00:11:09.989 --> 00:11:14.209
the structure before committing capital. Remember, you collect the fair, you do

00:11:14.209 --> 00:11:19.269
not buy the gas. Open the latest technical report for any royalty company you

00:11:19.269 --> 00:11:24.229
follow and locate the attributable production table, then divide the enterprise value by

00:11:24.229 --> 00:11:30.129
the 2027 attributable gold equivalent ounces to calculate an EV per ounce figure and note

00:11:30.129 --> 00:11:34.089
whether it sits above or below the sector median you recorded last quarter.

